# Every text file is stored and checked out with LF, on every OS.
#
# Prettier enforces `endOfLine: "lf"`. Without this file, a Windows clone with
# Git's default `core.autocrlf=true` checks everything out as CRLF, so
# `npm run format:check` fails on every file and hides the genuine failures.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary assets — never touch their bytes. `text=auto` would detect these
# anyway; naming them makes the intent explicit and guards against a file
# that happens to look like text.
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
*.png  binary
*.ico  binary
*.ttf  binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
*.pdf  binary
